<title>NETHERLANDS: Labouchere opens Dutch equities office in London.</title>
<headline>Labouchere opens Dutch equities office in London.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch financial services firm Labouchere said on Monday the Bank of England and the Securities and Futures Authority (SFA) had granted it formal permission to set up an office in London.</p>
<p>The office, which became operational today, will employ a team of Dutch and British specialists who will mainly market Dutch equities to institutional investors.</p>
<p>In June Labouchere hired six members of Dutch bank MeesPiersons' London equity sales team.</p>
<p>Labouchere, a unit of Dutch insurance group Aegon, already has offices in Amsterdam, New York, Geneva, Zurich and Luxembourg.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
